course: dictionary
lesson: 15398
title: Splitter: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A splitter comes from the word split, which means to break or divide something into parts. The most common meaning is a tool or device that splits something. «Mum used a splitter so that both headphones could plug into one phone.»
explain: Now look at the clues in the sentence. A phone and headphones are things, so the splitter is a device. But «Three players left the club to start their own team, and everyone called them splitters» is about people, so here a splitter is someone who leaves a group to form a new one.
explain: A splitter can also be a way of sorting. «Sam puts shells into tiny piles, so he is a splitter, not a lumper» is about dividing things into many small groups. A lumper does the opposite and puts things together into big groups.
explain: In sport, a splitter is a type of ball. «The bowler's splitter dropped sharply just before it reached the batter» tells you it is a delivery that drops or moves. The clue words are bowler and batter, which tell you it is a cricket or baseball word.
fact: A splitter is a noun, so it names a thing or a person.
fact: «Splitter» can mean a device that splits something, like a log splitter that chops firewood.
fact: In everyday UK slang, «splitter» can mean a person who leaves a group or party to form a new one.
fact: In sorting, a «splitter» divides things into many small groups, and the opposite is a «lumper».
fact: In cricket and baseball, a splitter is a throw or bowl that makes the ball drop or move.
exercise: «Mum plugged a splitter into the phone so two people could share the music.» What is a splitter here? | *A device that splits one signal into two | A cricket ball that drops | A sort of sweet | A person who leaves a group
exercise: «Three players left the club to start their own team, and everyone called them splitters.» What does splitter mean here? | A log-chopping machine | *A person who leaves a group to form a new one | A small pile of shells | A fast throw in baseball
exercise: Sam says, «I'm a splitter, not a lumper.» What does a splitter do when sorting things? | Joins them all into one big group | Throws them as far as possible | Hides them away | *Divides them into many small groups
test: «Lee used the log splitter to chop the firewood.» What does log splitter mean? | A bag for carrying firewood | A tree that grows tall | A person who sells wood | *A tool that splits logs apart
test: «The bowler's splitter dropped sharply just before it reached the batter.» In cricket, what is a splitter? | *A type of ball that drops or moves sharply | A fielder who runs very fast | An umpire's signal | A bat with a crack in it
exam: What does splitter mean in «Three friends were splitters, and they left the club to start their own»? | *A person who leaves a group to form a new one | A ball that drops in cricket | A person who sorts things into one big group | A machine for splitting wood
